1. Nf3 { [%eval 0.1] } { Overall lesson from game:
Don't go for absurd tactics unless you know for sure they work and have visualized the variation. Checks captures and threats always! } d5 { [%eval 0.18] } 2. d4 { [%eval 0.08] } Nf6 { [%eval 0.11] } 3. c4 { [%eval 0.22] } c6 { [%eval 0.24] } 4. e3 { [%eval 0.15] } e6 { [%eval 0.23] } 5. Nc3 { [%eval 0.16] } { B3 is the move against the semi slav setup } Nbd7 { [%eval 0.21] } 6. Qc2 { [%eval 0.18] } Bd6 { [%eval 0.17] } 7. Bd3 { [%eval 0.15] } O-O { [%eval 0.25] } 8. O-O { [%eval 0.33] } dxc4 { [%eval 0.27] } 9. Bxc4 { [%eval 0.33] } b5 { [%eval 0.37] } 10. Bd3 { [%eval 0.34] } Bb7 { [%eval 0.41] } 11. Rd1 { [%eval 0.11] } { the immediate e4 was better! I saw e4 in response but I could have played h3 afterwards, which was what I had planned anyways. } (11. e4 e5 12. h3 exd4 13. Nxd4 b4 14. Nf5 (14. Nce2) 14... bxc3 15. Nxd6 Ne5 16. Nxb7 Qxd3 17. Qxc3) 11... Qc7 { [%eval 0.3] } 12. e4 { [%eval 0.04] } (12. Bd2 { stronger was to develop quickly and go rac1, which I contemplated. E4 is slow now. After e4, e5, black has equalised. Playing for quick developement held an advantage as black's pieces are a little clumsy too. }) 12... e5 { [%eval 0.03] } 13. h3 { [%eval 0.08] } h6 { [%eval 0.34] } 14. Be3 { [%eval 0.44] } a6 { [%eval 0.48] } 15. Rac1 { [%eval 0.38] } Rac8 { [%eval 0.53] } 16. a4 { [%eval 0.33] } b4?! { [%eval 1.31] } { Inaccuracy. Qb8 was best. } (16... Qb8 17. Nxe5 Nxe5 18. dxe5 Bxe5 19. b4 Bh2+ 20. Kh1 Bf4 21. Qd2 Bxe3 22. Qxe3) 17. Ne2 { [%eval 0.81] } (17. dxe5 Nxe5 (17... Bxe5 18. Nxe5 Qxe5 (18... Nxe5 19. Nd5 Nxd5 20. exd5 Nxd3 21. Qxd3)) 18. Nxe5 Bxe5 19. Ne2 c5 20. f4 b3 21. Qxc5 Qxc5 22. Rxc5 Bc7 23. Rc4) 17... a5?! { [%eval 1.55] } { Inaccuracy. exd4 was best. } (17... exd4 18. Nexd4 Rfd8 19. Nf5 Bf8 20. Nd2 Ne5 21. Be2 c5 22. f3 Kh7 23. f4) 18. Bc4 { [%eval 1.51] } exd4 { [%eval 1.65] } 19. Nfxd4?! { [%eval 0.82] } { Inaccuracy. Nexd4 was best. } (19. Nexd4 Ne5 20. Nxe5 Bxe5 21. Nf3 Rcd8 22. Nxe5 Qxe5 23. Bd3 Rfe8 24. Bb6 Ra8) 19... Ne5? { [%eval 2.52] } { Mistake. Rfe8 was best. } (19... Rfe8 20. f3 Bf8 21. Kh1 Ne5 22. Bf4 Rcd8 23. Bh2 Rd7 24. Bb3 c5 25. Nb5) 20. Bb3 { [%eval 2.47] } Ng6 { [%eval 2.49] } 21. Nf5 { [%eval 2.14] } (21. e5 { e5! if Bxe5, then the knight hands. If nxd5, black's bishop is blocked from the b8-h2 diagonal and nf5 traps it } Nxe5 22. Nf5 Rfd8 23. f4 { black is losing a piece here. If ng3, nxd6 and the queen eyes the knight. If nd7, then the bishop hangs. } Nf3+ 24. gxf3) 21... Rfd8? { [%eval 3.78] } { Mistake. Bh2+ was best. } (21... Bh2+ 22. Kh1 c5 23. f3 Ba6 24. g3 c4 25. Ba2 Ne7 26. Bf4 Qa7 27. Nxe7+) 22. Bxh6?? { [%eval 0.28] } { Blunder. Bxf7+ was best. } (22. Bxf7+ { The key tactical shot:
- if king takes, the queen infiltrates with qb3 followed by qe6.
- If queen takes, the bishop hangs } Qxf7 (22... Kxf7 23. Qb3+ Ke8 (23... Kf8 24. Nxd6 Rxd6 25. Rxd6 Qxd6 (25... Qf7) 26. Bc5 { black can't go kf8 because of the pin at the end of the line }) 24. Qe6+ Kf8 25. Nxd6) 23. Nxd6 Rxd6 24. Rxd6 Ne5 25. Ng3 c5 26. f4 Neg4 27. hxg4 Nxg4) 22... gxh6 { [%eval 0.36] } 23. Nxh6+ { [%eval 0.34] } Kg7 { [%eval 0.44] } 24. Nxf7 { [%eval 0.34] } Bh2+ { [%eval 0.35] } 25. Kh1 { [%eval 0.36] } Rxd1+ { [%eval 0.55] } 26. Rxd1?! { [%eval -0.24] } { Inaccuracy. Qxd1 was best. } (26. Qxd1 Be5 27. f3 c5 28. Qd2 Bf4 29. Nxf4 Qxf4 30. Qxf4 Nxf4 31. Nd6 Nd3) 26... c5 { [%eval -0.23] } 27. Ng5 { [%eval -0.32] } Nf8?? { [%eval 1.68] } { Blunder. Re8 was best. } (27... Re8 28. Bd5 Bxd5 29. exd5 Qe5 30. Ne6+ Kf7 31. g3 Nxd5 32. Qxc5 Rxe6 33. Rxd5) 28. Be6?? { [%eval -1.22] } { Blunder. Qc4 was best. } { The only reason I played this was because I thought I had nd4 as a follow up! BUT THE QUEEN IS DEFENDED!!! } (28. Qc4 { qc4 is best. We threaten to win the bishop with g3 and black is almost paralyzed here. If be5, then f4! If bxf4, then trade and the queen is deflected from the defense of the f7 square. Often, my positional instinct gives me the best moves, rather than purely tactical calculation. Trust my positional instinct more. } Be5 (28... Kh6) 29. f4 Bxf4 30. Nxf4 Qxf4 31. Qf7+ Kh6 32. Qxb7 Rc7 33. Qb8 Kxg5) (28. Bc4) 28... Re8?! { [%eval -0.35] } { Inaccuracy. Nxe4 was best. } (28... Nxe4 29. Nxe4 Nxe6 30. f3 Rh8 31. g3 Rxh3 32. Kg2 Bxe4 33. Qxe4 Rxg3+ 34. Kxh2) 29. Nd4?? { [%eval -5.24] } { Blunder. Bf5 was best. } (29. Bf5 { bf5 is best, just keeping it simpler. } Bd6 30. Qc4 Re7 31. f4 Bxf4 32. Nxf4 Qxf4 33. Qxc5 Qe5 34. Qxe5 Rxe5) 29... cxd4 { [%eval -5.22] } 30. Qb3 { [%eval -6.56] } Bf4 { [%eval -6.21] } 31. Bf7 { [%eval -6.52] } Re7 { [%eval -6.73] } 32. Ne6+ { [%eval -7.66] } Nxe6 { [%eval -7.44] } 33. Bxe6 { [%eval -7.47] } Qe5 { [%eval -7.18] } 34. Bf5 { [%eval -8.3] } Bxe4 { [%eval -8.87] } 35. Bxe4 { [%eval -7.9] } Qxe4 { [%eva